    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d147-a1-a13-a6">

                <pb facs="0400" n="390" xml:id="pg390"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Enclosure 6 in No. 11.]</seg></opener>
                <head>Rear-Admiral Sir B. Walker to Sir P. Wodehouse.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">“Narcissus,” Simon’s
                            Bay,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-01-18"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >January</hi> 18, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Referring to your communication of the 9th
                    instant, relative to the inspection of the Conrad, lately called the Tuscaloosa,
                    I beg to enclose for your excellency’s information the report of the condition
                    of this vessel and her equipments made by Mr. J. Hoets (on the part of the
                    United States consul) and Lieutenant Kennedy and Mr. Pounds, master of her
                    Majesty’s ship Narcissus.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>B. W. WALKER.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
